name: Confirmed SARIF retains review provenance after source changes
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/confirmed_sarif.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled observation | retained-review
ask: Does Review keep the human confirmation and source-change limitations without treating the later observation as a fix or a new confirmation?
paste-file: @ART/shell-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CONFIRM · descriptor-declared effect | export-approval
require-shell: test ! -e @TMP_TARGET/shell-confirmed.sarif
keys: y
require-live-snap: 25 run receipt | native-shell-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/confirmed_sarif.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
ask: Does the real native export retain exactly one recorded confirmation, its authority and source basis, with explicit historical scope and no current-checkout assessment claim?
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled observation | returned-review
resize: 160x48
live-snap: review-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: review-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: review-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: review-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: review-40x12
expect: F-0001
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | finding-focus-40x12
expect: F-0001
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-40x12-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-40x12-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-40x12-page-3
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-40x12-page-4
keys: NPage
live-snap: decision-40x12-page-5
ask: At all six sizes, can the operator identify the retained observation and inspect its decision and source limitation without losing navigation?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled observation | returned-list
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled observation | no-color-review
resize: 160x48
live-snap: no-color-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: no-color-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: no-color-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: no-color-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: no-color-40x12
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/confirmed_sarif.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart retain the same two observations, one human decision and both report files, without additional work or source changes?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
